{
  "title": "Ευχαριστώ!",
  "translation": "Thank you!",
  "topics": "Two letters, one sound: αι, ει, οι, ου, αυ, ευ, μπ, ντ, γκ, γγ, τσ, τζ, and γι before a vowel",
  "interface": "english",
  "alphabet": true,
  "titles": {
    "grammar": "The letters",
    "use": "Practice",
    "vocabulary": "Words",
    "reading": "Read",
    "writing": "Write"
  },
  "keys": "αβγδεζηθικλμνξοπρστςυφχψωάέήίόύώ",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      "Some pairs of letters are read as one sound. They are very common: once you know them, there is almost nothing left to learn about reading Greek.",
      {
        "h": "Vowel pairs"
      },
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "αι",
            "latin": "e",
            "say": "like the e in bed: the same as ε",
            "word": "και",
            "word_latin": "ke",
            "meaning": "and"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ει",
            "latin": "i",
            "say": "like the ee in see",
            "word": "είμαι",
            "word_latin": "íme",
            "meaning": "I am"
          },
          {
            "letter": "οι",
            "latin": "i",
            "say": "also like the ee in see",
            "word": "οικογένεια",
            "word_latin": "ikoyénia",
            "meaning": "family"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ου",
            "latin": "u",
            "say": "like the oo in food",
            "word": "ουρανός",
            "word_latin": "uranós",
            "meaning": "sky"
          },
          {
            "letter": "αυ",
            "latin": "av / af",
            "say": "av before a vowel or β γ δ ζ λ μ ν ρ; af before θ κ ξ π σ τ φ χ ψ",
            "word": "αύριο",
            "word_latin": "ávrio",
            "meaning": "tomorrow"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ευ",
            "latin": "ev / ef",
            "say": "the same rule: ev or ef",
            "word": "ευχαριστώ",
            "word_latin": "efcharistó",
            "meaning": "thank you"
          }
        ],
        "lang": "el"
      },
      "So the sound *i* can be written in five ways (ι, η, υ, ει, οι) and the sound *e* in two (ε, αι). Again: you can always read a word, but you have to learn how to write it.",
      {
        "h": "Consonant pairs"
      },
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "μπ",
            "latin": "b",
            "say": "b at the start of a word; mb or b inside",
            "word": "μπύρα",
            "word_latin": "bíra",
            "meaning": "beer"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ντ",
            "latin": "d",
            "say": "d at the start of a word; nd or d inside",
            "word": "ντομάτα",
            "word_latin": "domáta",
            "meaning": "tomato"
          },
          {
            "letter": "γκ",
            "latin": "g",
            "say": "a hard g at the start of a word; ng or g inside",
            "word": "γκαράζ",
            "word_latin": "garáz",
            "meaning": "garage"
          },
          {
            "letter": "γγ",
            "latin": "ng",
            "say": "like the ng in finger",
            "word": "Αγγλία",
            "word_latin": "Anglía",
            "meaning": "England"
          },
          {
            "letter": "τσ",
            "latin": "ts",
            "say": "like the ts in cats",
            "word": "τσέπη",
            "word_latin": "tsépi",
            "meaning": "pocket"
          },
          {
            "letter": "τζ",
            "latin": "dz",
            "say": "like the ds in kids",
            "word": "τζάκι",
            "word_latin": "dzáki",
            "meaning": "fireplace"
          }
        ],
        "lang": "el"
      },
      "Greek has no single letters for the sounds *b*, *d* and *g*: that is why it uses these pairs, also in foreign words: *μπανάνα* (banána), *ντους* (dus, shower).",
      {
        "h": "γι before a vowel"
      },
      "When γι or γει comes before another vowel, it is read like a quick *y*: *γιαγιά* (yayá, grandma), *γεια* (ya, hi).",
      {
        "h": "Try reading"
      },
      "Read each word aloud, then tap it to check.",
      {
        "flash": [
          [
            "ευχαριστώ",
            "efcharistó",
            "thank you"
          ],
          [
            "και",
            "ke",
            "and"
          ],
          [
            "είμαι",
            "íme",
            "I am"
          ],
          [
            "ουρανός",
            "uranós",
            "sky"
          ],
          [
            "αύριο",
            "ávrio",
            "tomorrow"
          ],
          [
            "αυτό",
            "aftó",
            "this, it"
          ],
          [
            "μπύρα",
            "bíra",
            "beer"
          ],
          [
            "ντομάτα",
            "domáta",
            "tomato"
          ],
          [
            "γιαγιά",
            "yayá",
            "grandma"
          ],
          [
            "παιδί",
            "pedhí",
            "child"
          ],
          [
            "γεια",
            "ya",
            "hi, bye"
          ],
          [
            "τσέπη",
            "tsépi",
            "pocket"
          ]
        ],
        "lang": "el"
      }
    ]
  },
